ffmpeg-dmo (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Carry the frame_packing option of h264_metadata and hevc_metadata as
    FFmpeg pull request 25395 (https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/25395)
    has it after the review of 2026-10-31: patches 0010 to 0013 are replaced
    by the corrected series and 0068 is added after 0011. The first revision
    they carried had none of the corrections below, and its showinfo tests
    are gone with the old 0013 (the API tests replace them).
    - H.265: inserting an arrangement clears general_non_packed_constraint_flag
      and its sub-layer flag in the VPS and SPS, those of the extradata too
      (H.265 7.4.4, D.3.16); a layout given too late for the parameter sets
      already passed on is an error.
    - H.265: the SEI NAL unit written for a picture has the TemporalId and the
      layer of that picture (H.265 D.3.1; patch 0068 in cbs_sei).
    - H.264 and H.265: a new message ends the arrangements of other ids that
      are still in force, and a 2D description in H.265 ends them without a
      replacement (H.264 D.2.26, H.265 D.3.16); the self-contained flags follow
      the messages already seen in the coded video sequence.
    - H.264 and H.265: extraction no longer exports mirrored views or quincunx
      layouts that AVStereo3D cannot describe; removal also covers the
      extradata; the H.264 tile format needs a cropped size that is a multiple
      of 3 (H.264 D.2.26).
    - New FATE tests: cbs-h264-frame-packing, cbs-hevc-frame-packing,
      cbs-hevc-frame-packing-constraint and cbs-hevc-frame-packing-sublayers.
    - Patch 0010 also changes where a new H.264 SEI unit goes (in front of the
      IDR slice), as it did; the upstream reference of cbs-h264-metadata-sei
      follows it in the pull request and does not exist in 9.0.2.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@
